## Key Concepts

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Heap overflow** | Writing past a heap buffer into adjacent heap memory |
| **Function pointer** | A variable that holds the address of a function |
| **Heap metadata** | 8-byte header malloc places before each chunk |
| **Chunk adjacency** | Consecutive mallocs produce adjacent chunks in memory |
| **`argv[1]`** | Input via command line argument, not stdin |
| **`strcpy` unsafe** | No bounds check — copies until null byte regardless of size |